codex
The supplied semantics confirms the distinction: `FuncDef` creates `closureVal(params, body, definingEnv)`, while `#applyK` allocates a frame, binds the argument, executes `BODY`, and only then returns. I’m adding an independent syntax-tree comparison (no execution of the untrusted source) to verify the frozen rule’s parameter, decision tree, return leaves, and defining location against both `solution.py` and `solution.mpy`.
